4-602.13 The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) walk-in cooler shelves (beginning of mold buildup in some places);
B) storage rack for soda machine motor - located in cabinet below drink counter in lobby (moldy buildup); 
C) counter under tea maker on drink counter (sugar and debris);  and
D) counter behind soda machine at drink counter (dust/general buildup).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris

6-501.12 Floors were observed to be in need of detail cleaning in the following areas:
A) under ice machine (food/general debris on the floor and in the floor drain);
B) along the walls and in the corners under storage shelving for dry goods and clean dishes (general debris accumulation); 
C) along the walls and in the corners inside the walk-in cooler (general debris accumulation); and
D) lids under carbon dioxide tanks (general buildup).
Physical facilities shall be cleaned as often as necessary to keep them clean.
